Sure! Below is a simple HTML website that displays one of four random jokes when a user clicks a button.

### ✅ Features:
- 4 predefined jokes in a JavaScript array
- A button to trigger the joke display
- A random joke is shown each time the button is clicked

---

### ✅ Complete HTML Code:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Random Joke Generator</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            text-align: center;
            margin-top: 100px;
        }
        #joke {
            font-size: 1.2em;
            margin-top: 20px;
            color: #333;
        }
        button {
            padding: 10px 20px;
            font-size: 1em;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Random Joke Generator</h1>
    <button onclick="showRandomJoke()">Tell Me a Joke!</button>
    <div id="joke"></div>

    <script>
        const jokes = [
            "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!",
            "Why did the scarecrow win an award? Because he was outstanding in his field!",
            "What do you call a fake noodle? An impasta!",
            "Why did the bicycle fall over? Because it was two-tired!"
        ];

        function showRandomJoke() {
            const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length);
            const jokeText = jokes[randomIndex];
            document.getElementById("joke").textContent = jokeText;
        }
    </script>

</body>
</html>
```

---

### 💡 How to Use:
1. Save the code above in a file with the `.html` extension (e.g., `joke.html`).
2. Open the file in a web browser.
3. Click the **"Tell Me a Joke!"** button to see a random joke from the list.

